From 9de6073b2c7439090b32beb0d06c1fbc6a730744 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SovereignOS Build <build@sovereignos.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:44:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 78/89] sovereignos: drop the artificial delay before redeeming the
 active-dismiss grant

Real hardware testing found the authorized-branch dismiss, while it
successfully eliminated the swipe, still reused the unauthorized
branch's 500ms delay -- producing a perceptible pause between typing
the decoy PIN and landing, distinguishable from a real same-user
unlock (which the owner confirmed lands immediately, PIN typed into
an already-showing bouncer). That 500ms exists in stock AOSP to let a
*freshly shown* bouncer's own async layout listeners settle before
interaction; this branch never shows a bouncer at all, so the race it
guards against does not apply here.

Changed postDelayed(..., 500) to postDelayed(..., 0), keeping the
handler-posted ordering (still delivered after the switch's own
response, matching DecoyProfileHelper's own established rationale for
posting rather than calling inline) and the mDismissToken tagging (so
this callback remains cancellable by the existing
removeCallbacksAndMessages(mDismissToken) path if an intervening
switch supersedes it), while removing the specific 500ms wait that
has no equivalent justification in this branch.

This does not eliminate the switch machinery's own latency (~865ms
from credential-verified to onUserSwitchComplete) or the transition
animation (~830ms) observed on real hardware for the previous
candidate -- those are inherent to this being a real user switch, not
an artificial pause this patch can remove. Unvalidated on hardware as
of this commit; needs a real touch-input trial before being treated
as confirmed, same as the swipe-elimination change itself was.
---
 .../keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java        | 26 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
index 303977013de5..b8f814be4aa6 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
@@ -796,16 +796,26 @@ public class KeyguardViewMediator implements CoreStartable,
                     // next gesture happens to request a bouncer, which is the one place the third
                     // (active-dismiss) grant from the same mint gets redeemed (see
                     // UserController#consumeDecoySwitchAuthorizationForActiveDismiss).
-                    // Proactively requesting the same dismiss here, on the same delay, redeems
-                    // that still-outstanding grant immediately instead of leaving it to a
-                    // gesture: it goes through the identical showNextSecurityScreenOrFinish()
-                    // chokepoint trust-agent and biometric dismissals already use, gated on the
-                    // same single-use, credential-verified authorization this exact switch
-                    // already earned -- not a new dismiss authority, just triggering the existing
-                    // one proactively.
+                    // Proactively requesting the same dismiss here redeems that still-outstanding
+                    // grant immediately instead of leaving it to a gesture: it goes through the
+                    // identical showNextSecurityScreenOrFinish() chokepoint trust-agent and
+                    // biometric dismissals already use, gated on the same single-use,
+                    // credential-verified authorization this exact switch already earned -- not a
+                    // new dismiss authority, just triggering the existing one proactively.
+                    // Deliberately posted with a 0ms delay, unlike the unauthorized branch
+                    // above's 500ms: that delay exists to let a *freshly shown* bouncer's own
+                    // async layout listeners settle before it is interacted with (stock AOSP
+                    // behavior, predating this patch) -- this branch never shows a bouncer at
+                    // all, so that race does not apply, and a real same-user unlock (PIN typed
+                    // into an already-showing bouncer) is not held to any such delay either.
+                    // Still routed through postDelayed (not a bare post()), and still tagged
+                    // with mDismissToken, so this callback is cancellable the same way the
+                    // unauthorized branch's already is (see removeCallbacksAndMessages(
+                    // mDismissToken) above) if an intervening switch supersedes it before this
+                    // runs.
                     mHandler.postDelayed(
                             () -> dismiss(null /* callback */, null /* message */), mDismissToken,
-                            500);
+                            0);
                 }
             }
         }
